// Pull request: #6166 feat: Add PUA - TruffleHog Execution macOS rule
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6166
// Pull request author: Breakingpoint608
// Change: new rule
// Title: PUA - TruffleHog Execution - macOS
// Sigma ID: 89342720-1682-492a-9d2d-ba34db0df713
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Ritika (IsThisRitika)
// Date: 2026-07-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, credential-access, T1083, T1552.001
// Description: Detects execution of TruffleHog, a tool used to search for secrets in different platforms like
//   Git, Jira, Slack, SharePoint, etc. that could be used maliciously. While it is a legitimate
//   tool, intended for use in CI pipelines and security assessments, It was observed in the Shai-
//   Hulud malware campaign targeting npm packages to steal sensitive information.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of TruffleHog by security teams or developers.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog
//   - https://www.getsafety.com/blog-posts/shai-hulud-npm-attack
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/7422ce3b9d2f60cc3cff8fe917654e4534e1efd5/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_pua_trufflehog.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/trufflehog" or ((ProcessCommandLine contains " docker --image " or ProcessCommandLine contains " Git " or ProcessCommandLine contains " GitHub " or ProcessCommandLine contains " Jira " or ProcessCommandLine contains " Slack " or ProcessCommandLine contains " Confluence " or ProcessCommandLine contains " SharePoint " or ProcessCommandLine contains " s3 " or ProcessCommandLine contains " gcs ") and ProcessCommandLine contains " --results=verified")
